<title>FINLAND: Aker Maritime unit wins FIM 100 mln deal.</title>
<headline>Aker Maritime unit wins FIM 100 mln deal.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norwegian Offshore group Aker Maritime ASA's Finnish subsidiary Aker Rauma Offshore has won a contract to transport a Russian oilrig from Bahrain to the Caspian Sea, its managing director, Risto Neuvo, said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The value of the order from Russian company Lukoil was 100 million markka ($20.4 million), Neuvo told Reuters.</p>
<p>Aker Rauma will coordinate transport to Finland and onwards, take the rig apart in Finland and manage reassembly in the Caspian Sea, using sub-contractors for the shipping and other stages of the project, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Likely there will also be an additional deal to upgrade the oilrig,&quot; Neuvo said. The rig has been used for production but will be rebuilt for exploration, he added.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247 ($ = 4.900 Finnish Markka)</p>
</text>
